# Django Clean Architecture

## Reglas de capas

| Capa | Puede importar | No puede importar |
|------|----------------|-------------------|
| `domain/` | stdlib, typing | django, rest_framework, celery |
| `application/` | domain | django ORM directo |
| `infrastructure/` | domain, application, django, drf | — |

## Patrón por feature

```python
# domain/services.py — lógica pura
class OrderStateMachine:
    def transition(self, current: OrderStatus, target: OrderStatus) -> OrderStatus:
        if target not in VALID_TRANSITIONS[current]:
            raise InvalidTransitionError(...)
        return target

# application/use_cases/create_order.py
class CreateOrderUseCase:
    def __init__(self, repo: OrderRepository): ...
    def execute(self, dto: CreateOrderDTO) -> Order: ...

# infrastructure/repositories.py
class DjangoOrderRepository(OrderRepository):
    def save(self, order: Order) -> Order:
        model = OrderModel.from_entity(order)
        model.save()
        return model.to_entity()
```

## Django apps

Cada feature = Django app en `features/<name>/` con `apps.py` y label único.

## Tests obligatorios

```
features/<modulo>/tests/
├── domain/           # Sin DB
├── application/      # Mocks de repos
└── infrastructure/   # pytest-django + APIClient
```
